# Baseline: shani-desktop-plasma Saturn theming on Plasma 6.7
#
# PURPOSE: the package builds fine even when the theme renders wrong, so
# there is no build-time signal for a theming regression. This file is the
# known-good state to diff a future run against. Any RESULT line that is not
# PASS is the regression.
#
# HOW TO USE (after Plasma 6.8 lands):
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/pkg:ro" archlinux:latest bash -c '
#     pacman -Sy --noconfirm
#     pacman -S --noconfirm --needed --overwrite "*" plasma-desktop \
#       plasma-workspace kwin-x11 kvantum kde-gtk-config breeze-gtk dolphin \
#       konsole yakuake fish gtk3-demos gtk4-demos wmctrl xorg-server-xvfb \
#       xdotool imagemagick discover plasma-systemmonitor kate kcalc
#     SCREEN=1920x1080 bash /pkg/tests/plasma-session.sh Saturn-Dark /tmp/shots' \
#   | grep "^RESULT" > /tmp/new.result
#   diff <(grep "^RESULT" tests/baseline-plasma-6.7.result) /tmp/new.result
#
# CAPTURED: 2026-09-26 03:36 UTC
# PLASMA:   plasma-workspace 6.7.5-1 (Arch extra; version confirmed with
#           `pacman -Si`, not assumed)
# HARNESS:  tests/plasma-session.sh Saturn-Dark, package tree at /pkg
# EXITS:    PACMAN_EXIT=0, HARNESS_EXIT=0
#
# SCOPE LIMIT: Saturn-Dark only. Saturn and Saturn-Twilight are NOT
# baselined - run all three looks before concluding anything about the
# theme, then add them here.
#
# NOT CAPTURED: the screenshots. The container was --rm and the harness wrote
# them to an unmounted path, so only the RESULT lines survive. Re-capture
# with a mounted output directory if the visual evidence is needed.

